==English==
{{wikipedia|convolution}}
{{wikipedia|convolution (computer science)}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|convolutus||to roll together}}, past participle of {{m|la|convolvere}}, from {{m|la|con-}} + {{m|la|volvere||to roll}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|uːʃən|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Something that is [[folded]] or [[twisted]].
# Any of the [[fold]]s on the [[surface]] of the [[brain]].
# The shape of something [[rotating]]; a [[vortex]].
# {{label|en|mathematics}} A form of [[moving]] [[average]].
# {{label|en|computing}} A function which maps a [[tuple]] of [[sequences]] into a sequence of tuples.

